      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T01:43:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "JJ doesn\u0027t use the raw JJ change ID as the change ID to upload to gerrit.\n\nhttps://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/blob/89b514f74e9b0eef72b20be58c417583cec7f8eb/cli/src/commands/gerrit/upload.rs#L600\n\nWith the current code here, when we eventually drop the part where we add change IDs to gerrit automatically for you, it will change the gerrit change-ID of existing commits, and thus disassociate commits.\n\nCould you use the same mechanism we use to generate the change IDs so that the change IDs you calculate are consistent with those generated by jj and thus backwards compatible",
      "revId": "17c127e740db54df6973d19b2757dac95c3a46fa",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3eb4c1ec_df44abb6",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/util/JujutsuChangeIdUtil.java",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1155599
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T06:54:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As you say, the intention here would then be to contribute to the `jj gerrit upload` an option to not create a `Change-Id` footer, which would eventually become the default once we deem Gerrit\u0027s support for JJ change-id to be good enough. I already have such patch in my fork of JJ and I\u0027ll polish it and contribute it upstream once this series is merged.\n\nHowever, if a `Change-Id` footer is present, it will take priority over the header, so if you have ongoing work you can simply keep the `Change-Id` in the footer and your change will stay the same.\n\nDoes this answer your concern?",
      "parentUuid": "d3042c50_2d2dc620",
      "revId": "17c127e740db54df6973d19b2757dac95c3a46fa",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
